 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Most oil paints take about year to fully cure. I usually recommend waiting at least six months. Then do a quick test with a hairdryer. Leave it on one spot for fifteen seconds, if it' still shiny, wait a bit longer. If you' in a rush, a thin coat of lacquer or a clear varnish can give the finish a week or so of protection. It should feel smooth and slightly dull, not shiny like fresh paint. Gentle touch tests with your fingernail don't leave mark.",
